Issues
------
* tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni (+2/-0/=F0=9F=92=AC0)
  2 issues created:
  - split-mode may be more a three-way thing than a two-way thing (by sftcd)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/issues/516=20
  - we could have better guidance for construction of client hello outer 2 =
in case of HRR (by sftcd)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/issues/515=20

* tlswg/dtls13-spec (+1/-0/=F0=9F=92=AC0)
  1 issues created:
  - Mention RFC 7457 in Security section (by elvey)
    https://github.com/tlswg/dtls13-spec/issues/254=20



Pull requests
-------------
* tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni (+1/-5/=F0=9F=92=AC20)
  1 pull requests submitted:
  - Ensure Inner CH is smaller or equal in size to Outer CH (by dennisjacks=
on)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/514=20

  4 pull requests received 20 new comments:
  - #514 Abort on duplicate OuterExtensions (16 by chris-wood, cjpatton, da=
vidben, dennisjackson, sftcd)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/514=20
  - #497 Try clarify an odd MUST in 6.1.5 (1 by sftcd)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/497=20
  - #495 optional configids seems wrong, maybe random is better? (1 by sftc=
d)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/495=20
  - #492 Bit more text on nominal backend processing (2 by chris-wood, sftc=
d)
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/492=20

  5 pull requests merged:
  - Add -12 changelog.
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/482=20
  - Abort on duplicate OuterExtensions
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/514=20
  - Rework Handshaking with ClientHelloInner to remove conflicts and...
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/508=20
  - retry configs: tweak about subsequent connections=20
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/498=20
  - optional configids seems wrong, maybe random is better?
    https://github.com/tlswg/draft-ietf-tls-esni/pull/495=20

* tlswg/tls13-spec (+1/-0/=F0=9F=92=AC0)
  1 pull requests submitted:
  - Clarifying the security properties of 0-RTT data. (by nimia)
    https://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/1236=20

* tlswg/dtls13-spec (+1/-0/=F0=9F=92=AC2)
  1 pull requests submitted:
  - Increase effective epoch width to 64 bits, keeping the serialized repre=
sentation 16 bits wide (by chris-wood)
    https://github.com/tlswg/dtls13-spec/pull/255=20

  1 pull requests received 2 new comments:
  - #255 Increase effective epoch width to 64 bits, keeping the serialized =
representation 16 bits wide (2 by chris-wood, ekr)
    https://github.com/tlswg/dtls13-spec/pull/255=20


